list the Switch Online Game Boy palettes

This changes what the Palette row offers rather than making upstream
work here, and it only does anything with the matching mGBA core patch
(cores/mgba/patches/gb-nso-palettes.patch).

slot never sends mGBA a colour, only the name of one of the core's
presets, and GbPalette is the hard-coded list of those names. mGBA
cannot load a palette from a file, so the two shades of green that
Nintendo's Game Boy app on Switch Online uses for its original and
Pocket looks can only be offered by adding them to both lists. This is
the slot half: "NSO DMG" and "NSO Pocket", placed after "GB Light" so
the monochrome palettes stay together and SELECT + L2 / R2 reaches them
in a short walk from the default.

The list is walked by name, and slot_state.txt stores the name, so
nothing saved moves. A core built without the patch ignores a name it
does not know and keeps the previous palette, so a mismatched pair
degrades to a palette that does not change rather than a crash.

